{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts","id":1556176,"title":"Non-Bound supernaturals generating ghosts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-05T11:36:13-08:00","id":1556176,"title":"Non-Bound supernaturals generating ghosts?","content":"Not all supernatural have souls, or else possess them no longer. Examples includes Beasts (whole soul is replaced by the Horror) or a mummy (whose soul fractured five ways).<br /> <br /> But ghosts aren't souls!<br /> <br /> COULD a supernatural generate a ghost? By dying. An NDE? Bizarre magical ect? How would such a ghost diverge from the norm? Would they 'remember' being something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T12:01:37-08:00","id":1556179,"title":"","content":"There's offhand mentions of ghosts of supernatural creatures in 1e's books for Vampire, Werewolf, and Promethean, and more involved discussion in Mage; a case can be made for 1e Changeling including the Gravewight kith with no special notes that changelings might similarly be valid there, whereas it's a pretty distinct metaphysical point for demons to not have anything like a guaranteed afterlife (though the human former tenants of soul pacted Covers can potentially reappear as Echoes); mummies being what they are, it's unlikely for them to produce ghosts that are actually bits of themselves, and the Unfettered Inheritance kind of takes the narrative space a ghost would for Beasts; Hunters are mortals and thus theoretically as capable of leaving ghosts as any human is, while deviants are a sufficiently broad umbrella that they might or might not create one depending on their circumstances.<br /> <br /> In 2e, most things that don't run on Integrity or Wisdom can probably be assumed not to directly make work for the ghost-specific gameline now that the Underworld and its primary interfacing splat are known to exist, much like how we haven't gotten &quot;hunters&quot; as a dedicated slot in the list of Antagonists in a splatbook since Hunter came out as a gameline. Any exceptions are by definition going to be exceptional, but the trends of ghosts as a whole are such that their memories are at least a little Swiss-cheesed as is typical.<br /> <br /> Ghosts created by someone's own death use the character's own Integrity, while the ghosts of objects and animals derive their initial power from the Integrity of human referents; it may be that there's a similar phenomenon to the lack of directly human-derived spirits in the Shadow, or there could instead be a shortcut like the Graveyard Geist phenomenon that allows something that doesn't have Integrity but does have humanlike intelligence to leave a ghost. The salient point for Geist's purposes still largely boils down to trauma and loss, and any supernatural qualities beyond echoing the thing's former powers are going to depend on the storyhook that's responsible for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T12:15:18-08:00","id":1556181,"title":"","content":"No, I don't mean powers, just memories of what they think they 'once were' .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:03:11-08:00","id":1556190,"title":"","content":"First: Mummies don't have fractured souls. Aside from being claimed as slaves by the Judges, their souls are just fine. The Pillars aren't a fracture, but <i>an understanding</i> about souls. Everyone with a full soul has the five of them, as far as Mummies understand it, it just doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> That said, the game isn't <i>completely</i> clear on what ghosts in general are. They're memories, but also something else, and they can be either memories of the destroyed person/thing or memories <i>about</i> it, which complicates things even more.<br /> <br /> In the end the answer is yes, although they would be rare and mostly defined by the ST. A supernatural is far less likely to leave a ghost and this ghost won't be anything special compared to other ghosts.<br /> <br /> Overall ghosts form as a response to Integrity, and the type of trauma it represents, so entities without Integrity are unlikely to produce ghosts. The presence of a soul may also be a factor, even the ghost not being the soul itself (or at least not <i>all</i> of it, that's still under debate). Leaving something else behind also probably reduces the likelihood of a ghost forming, as those memories can still &quot;coalesce&quot; on something. A torpid corpse, an echo that can come back from death, a dream of itself, things that in a sense already fit the trope of a ghost.<br /> <br /> Yet, humans can, very rarely, form ghosts without dying. So there's precedence for anything to happen, even if not an appreciable probability.<br /> <br /> My personal take is that the least likely splat to leave a ghost of any sort, even if completely destroyed, are Demons, as both their memories and the memories about them are too tied to their Covers. It's possible, though, that a Cover do leave a ghost sometimes, if not one likely to know the nature of the Demon (but who knows?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:48:05-08:00","id":1556199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556181#post1556181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't mean powers, just memories of what they think they 'once were' .</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. See &quot;Any exceptions are by definition going to be exceptional, but the trends of ghosts as a whole are such that their memories are at least a little Swiss-cheesed as is typical.&quot; This is a class of being empowered by living people remembering it as it used to be, which any supernatural powers it didn't gain from &quot;becoming&quot; a ghost are necessarily informed by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T05:51:31-08:00","id":1556340,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Mummies can for, and their near death experiences seem to end with them returning on another mission for the Judges. So I'm a no for them.<br /> <br /> Mages have always had a thing about ghost-mages able to use Numina which looks like the rote spells/praxes they had in life, but losing most of their power. So at least having a possibility of leaving a ghost seems guaranteed.<br /> <br /> Vampires are arguably already dead, and may or may not leave a ghost, though iirc in both editions they can survive in the Underworld without blood (though there is a river of blood) by eating ghosts... Though it can become addictive. So I'm fine with no ghost of vampires - but you could have a ghost left after the embrace changes them I to a vampire; this one is entirely contestable, but I'm happy with my answer.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have no reason not to leave ghost, imo. They are said to be disconnected from the human collective unconscious, and sometimes dream their way to the Anima Mundi, so arguably their half-spirit nature (and I don't think spiritsleave ghosts) may disqualify them. So if you wanted you could have it depend on their harmony (like make a roll where very spirit leaning werewolves are unlikely to leave a ghost, but human-leaning werewolves are likely...).<br /> <br /> Hunter are human so why not? Slashers have lost their humanity so I'm liable to make them like Vampires (having created a ghost when they lost it) but I suppose they could create a ghost if a human's integrity was affected by their death...<br /> <br /> Changlings are in a similar boat to werewolves, their souls are twisted but they are still fairly human. Maybe high Wyrd changlings are more likely to become some kind of hedge entity/goblin? I'm not sure what fits them best.<br /> <br /> Demons can not leave ghosts, but as above, i love the idea that their covers can.<br /> <br /> Which leaves Deviants and Prometheans. Deviants i don't know enough about, but again, those that were human have had their souls torn apart, your milage may vary. Prometheans are sometimes may from human bodies, so theremaybea ghost ofwhatthey were previously, and they can become a normal human as their reward/after-life. But they can experience death and return from the Underworld (at least once again) so I am leaning towards no.<br /> <br /> Also, Bound are described as already being ghosts, so they can't leave a ghost, though may become one of they manage to die.<br /> <br /> --<br /> EDIT: but disregarding all of the above. The correct answers is, what makes the most sense for your game. <br /> <br /> Is it more fun of you have Vampire ghosts moping around? Then go for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-08-2025, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T10:13:58-08:00","id":1556347,"title":"","content":"Vampire ghosts? Say hello to the Hollow Mekhet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:28:07-08:00","id":1556382,"title":"","content":"Shadows aren't Ghosts, are they? Living in mirrors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:37:37-08:00","id":1556383,"title":"","content":"Who can say? Ghosts are Ephemeral Entities, and thus 'normal' rules of existence don't apply to them. Kindred know such little nothing of the other Realms that the Hollow Mekhet's Shadow is probably right there in Twilight, it just can only be seen by its attached vampire in very specific manners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:08:09-08:00","id":1556388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556340#post1556340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm a no for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a hard no for any splat, really.<br /> <br /> Edge cases and weird mysteries are the staple of the setting. Whatever the standard situation is, or the likelihood of something, in principle there's always a way for it to happen if it isn't outright impossible for some very specific reason.<br /> <br /> And given that ghosts are formed by memories, and even objects, animals and still living humans leave ghosts, there's no reason for a ghost of any splat at all to be flat out impossible, as unlikely as it is.<br /> <br /> That said, I would have the most unlikely cases be Mummies (there's no shock in their death and they keep living), Werewolves (they're more likely to become something in the Shadow rather than a regular ghost), Bound (they're already ghosts) and Demons (their own identity has too little weight compared to their Covers, even for themselves).<br /> <br /> Hunters, Mages and Changelings I think would have a normal-ish chance. Changelings may have a harder time because Clarity instead of Integrity/Wisdom, but otherwise no big deal.<br /> <br /> Prometheans and Deviants are variable. They have unstable souls, which isn't a defining factor, but has some influence. Some are arguably more human than humans, others are almost lost to inhumanity, but overall their journey is really marked by relationship with their threads of humanity.<br /> <br /> Vampires literally have Humanity as a trait, so the same applies, but one important thing is added: memory. They're immortals with a close relationship to history and memory, theirs and from others in general. I think the older the Vampire, actually the more likely they are to leave a ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T10:38:57-08:00","id":1556398,"title":"","content":"Pronetheans yet to achieve their Great Work have no souls. Wouldn't that eliminate the possibility of ghosts forming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T11:45:44-08:00","id":1556400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556398#post1556398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pronetheans yet to achieve their Great Work have no souls. Wouldn't that eliminate the possibility of ghosts forming?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, since animals and objects can leaves ghosts (Barghest and Castoffs respectively) and neither of them have souls...<br /> <br /> So that question is whether it would be a unique kind of ghost, or it the Promethean isn't a singular solid entity which leaves a memory imprint like normal folks (a butter knife isn't going to leave the same weight as a sacrificial dagger, probably meaning the Castoff from the dagger ends up bring higher rank). <br /> <br /> Like you could theorize that Promethean's unstable nature - which tends to erode the fabric of reality and they draw energy from nature itself - is not conducive to leaving an imprint. But then they explicitly leaves imprinted memories in the Azothic Memory by doing things like creating Anathors... So maybe that is what a Promethean 'ghost' looks like... And that when they die their Azoth is released and burns away any memory imprint not contained in an Anathor.<br /> <br /> And if that works well for your game, my last rule is go with what makes your game the most interesting/fun.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you could have a Promethean leave a ghost/Castoff (depending on what they are made from...) as usual depending on what impact the death has on a human's integrity, but said ghost doesn't have any memories from the Promethean, it is just a Castoff of the materials used to construct the Promethean... I think a Mage game would find this an interesting Mystery to investigate; but what works for a Geist game is another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T11:47:17-08:00","id":1556401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556388#post1556388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a hard no for any splat, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand by my original edit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edge cases and weird mysteries are the staple of the setting. </div> </div> </div>What is your game trying to explore? What interesting themes are at play that you want to explore? Where is the horror aspect?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T12:22:27-08:00","id":1556404,"title":"","content":"What is the horror element of every new mage Awakening in Tawoomba, Australia generating a ghost upon signing their name on their Watchtower?<br /> <br /> Sometimes, something just <i>is</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T17:34:27-08:00","id":1556450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556398#post1556398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pronetheans yet to achieve their Great Work have no souls. Wouldn't that eliminate the possibility of ghosts forming?</div> </div> </div> </div>On top of souls not being a requirement, only making it more likely, they do have something that goes for a soul, the Divine Fire. And by its own nature, the Divine Fire does <i>things</i>, all sorts of things whatsoever. So there's something that may or may not help the formation of a ghost, or may hinder it, or may be even better at helping it than an actual soul, or may induce something else to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556401#post1556401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by my original edit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What is your game trying to explore? What interesting themes are at play that you want to explore? Where is the horror aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just added my own take and I didn't ask for a lecture on how to ST.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand the setting I see no need, and indeed no benefit, from a hard no for them. If I'll use on a game is another matter entirely.<br /> <br /> The game isn't just horror, by the way, it's more focused on mystery and the strange. While prominent, horror is an optional take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T17:49:28-08:00","id":1556451,"title":"","content":"And don't forget Tawoomba, Australia. <i>Every mage who Awakens in Tawoomba has their own ghost haunting them</i>. That's not horror, that's a Mystery, as the mages are in no real danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T19:29:02-08:00","id":1556455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556451#post1556451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't forget Tawoomba, Australia. <i>Every mage who Awakens in Tawoomba has their own ghost haunting them</i>. That's not horror, that's a Mystery, as the mages are in no real danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>We shall set aside the questionable nature of that statement for a moment and instead observe that the ghosts in question are Rank 1 (i.e. damaged enough to be overtly stuck in a pattern), are immune to Essence Bleed (i.e. are not geographically bound by Anchors), are trying to get their new Awakened selves to adhere to the patterns of their old Sleeper lives (i.e. are drawing attention to a group of people who have good reason to avoid attention), and are part of a larger phenomenon in Toowoomba that means <i>Sleepers</i> are also producing ghosts at a greater rate than usual and that ghost mages of the has-Arcana-and-uses-them variety are produced whenever a mage dies, all of which means that a) the local Consilium structure is so bent out of whack that <i>the Guardians of the Veil</i>, the typically <i>least populous </i>Order in the Diamond, are the <i>largest</i> Order in the area, and b) they <i>still</i> have their hands full with these circumstances that are also taking up the time of the two Pentacle Orders who aren't actively trying to take advantage of the situation to shock the populace into Awakening.<br /> <br /> And, lest we forget what gameline this thread concerns, <i>ghosts manifesting is seldom good for your Integrity</i>. The cancellation of <i>Fallen Worlds</i> means we didn't get a lot of new metaphysics content for the setting, including ghost-related stuff, but unless you are extremely optimistic about the attitude of a disproportionately large number of Doppelg\u00e4ngers arising in one city this looks like an Undertaker's nightmare. <i>Plasm is what lifts the knife. Plasm is what throws it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot to denote the placement of b). 12-11-2025, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T09:17:10-08:00","id":1556476,"title":"","content":"Mages have Wisdom, not Integrity. Ghosts being real poses no psychological issue to mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T09:32:27-08:00","id":1556477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556476#post1556476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have Wisdom, not Integrity. Ghosts being real poses no psychological issue to mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that there are characters besides mages in Toowoomba and that casting spells in front of most of them <i>is</i> bad for Wisdom, not least because it's bad for <i>their </i>Integrity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T17:25:09-08:00","id":1556486,"title":"","content":"None of this changes that this plot isn't necessarily &quot;horror&quot; as far as genre goes, especially given that Mage in general is even less focused on horror than most of CofD, lowering the fear effect of most things in the setting when looked upon through their lenses. For whatever it even means for the game in general as any particular chronicle can pertain to any genre whatsoever with the very same setting, rules and tools.<br /> <br /> But yeah, as this is a very big problem that affects the city as a whole and draws a lot of attention, I'd say Mages in Toowoomba are in quite some danger due to the ghost mystery.<br /> <br /> That said, danger has nothing to do with horror. Danger is an effective dramatic tool in any genre, but isn't strictly required. The only genre really defined by danger is action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T17:25:32-08:00","id":1556487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556450#post1556450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just added my own take and I didn't ask for a lecture on how to ST.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand the setting I see no need, and indeed no benefit, from a hard no for them. If I'll use on a game is another matter entirely.<br /> <br /> The game isn't just horror, by the way, it's more focused on mystery and the strange. While prominent, horror is an optional take.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't meant as a lecture, and apologies if it came across that way.<br /> <br /> I think originally i was more leaning on hard answers (whether yes or no), but my edit was to take a different approach. Answer the question by asking what story you are trying to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T19:05:30-08:00","id":1556496,"title":"","content":"Apologies accepted and I also ask them if my response was too rude.<br /> <br /> While it didn't sound good, my reaction may have been affected by recent changes in my medication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T12:30:01-08:00","id":1556534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556398#post1556398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pronetheans yet to achieve their Great Work have no souls. Wouldn't that eliminate the possibility of ghosts forming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage - Tome of the Pentacle states:<br /> <br /> <b>Despite Sleepers\u2019 beliefs, ghosts aren\u2019t actually the souls of the dead. They\u2019re echoes of people changed by traumatic events</b><br /> <br /> I would say that Prometheans count enough as people for this to work. Perhaps you might restrict it to some Promethean very close to the Great Work, but even animals can leave a ghost (albeit quite rarely) so I don't see &quot;having a soul&quot; as a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T20:03:56-08:00","id":1556820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1556176-non-bound-supernaturals-generating-ghosts?p=1556496#post1556496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies accepted and I also ask them if my response was too rude.<br /> 